<paragraph id="D32C36F7FFA85D4F48F2FF1A28CEFEBC" blockId="6.[151,1437,150,357]" pageId="6" pageNumber="123">
<emphasis id="E1E7EAE5FFA85D4F48F2FF1A2B60FF69" bold="true" box="[199,600,150,180]" pageId="6" pageNumber="123">
Calling song (1♁, 28.3°C) (
<figureCitation id="4BA82A72FFA85D4F4A31FF1A2B72FF69" box="[516,586,150,176]" captionStart="FIGURE 5" captionStartId="6.[151,250,1399,1423]" captionTargetBox="[162,1425,392,1365]" captionTargetId="figure-122@6.[151,1436,381,1376]" captionTargetPageId="6" captionText="FIGURE 5. Macroxiphus sumatranus ♁ calling song recorded in the laboratory: oscillograms showing six isolated echemes (A) and one echeme (B), and spectrogram of the same echeme (C)." figureDoi="http://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10692723" httpUri="https://zenodo.org/record/10692723/files/figure.png" pageId="6" pageNumber="123">Fig. 5</figureCitation>
).
</emphasis>
The calling song is made up of a fairly isolated echeme, each consisting of two closely-spaced syllables. Each echeme has an average duration of 0.35±0.02 s (0.33–0.37 s). The first syllable has an average duration of 18.7±0.9 ms (17.6–19.9 ms) and an average period of 0.15±0.01 s (0.14–0.16 s). The second syllable has an average duration of 18.9±1.2 ms (17.8–20.7 ms). The interval between the two syllables has an average duration of 0.13±0.01 s (0.11–0.14 s). The call spectrum is broad-based and has a peak frequency of 11.7±1.0 kHz (10.8–13.4 kHz).
</paragraph>
<caption id="87EC667FFFA85D4F48A2FAFB2A2DFA6D" ID-DOI="http://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10692723" ID-Zenodo-Dep="10692723" httpUri="https://zenodo.org/record/10692723/files/figure.png" pageId="6" pageNumber="123" startId="6.[151,250,1399,1423]" targetBox="[162,1425,392,1365]" targetPageId="6" targetType="figure">
<paragraph id="D32C36F7FFA85D4F48A2FAFB2A2DFA6D" blockId="6.[151,1436,1399,1460]" pageId="6" pageNumber="123">
<emphasis id="E1E7EAE5FFA85D4F48A2FAFB282AFA49" bold="true" box="[151,274,1399,1424]" pageId="6" pageNumber="123">FIGURE 5.</emphasis>
<taxonomicName id="14934D74FFA85D4F4922FAFB2B2FFA56" baseAuthorityName="Haan" baseAuthorityYear="1843" box="[279,535,1399,1423]" class="Insecta" family="Tettigoniidae" genus="Macroxiphus" kingdom="Animalia" order="Orthoptera" pageId="6" pageNumber="123" phylum="Arthropoda" rank="species" species="sumatranus">
<emphasis id="E1E7EAE5FFA85D4F4922FAFB2B2FFA56" box="[279,535,1399,1423]" italics="true" pageId="6" pageNumber="123">Macroxiphus sumatranus</emphasis>
</taxonomicName>
♁ calling song recorded in the laboratory: oscillograms showing six isolated echemes (A) and one echeme (B), and spectrogram of the same echeme (C).
</paragraph>
</caption>
<paragraph id="D32C36F7FFA85D4F48F2F98A2C0EF9B1" blockId="6.[151,1437,1542,1640]" pageId="6" pageNumber="123">
The calling song of the male from PFR consists of two syllables, similar to that of 
<taxonomicName id="14934D74FFA85D4F4C4BF98A2822F99A" baseAuthorityName="Haan" baseAuthorityYear="1843" class="Insecta" family="Tettigoniidae" genus="Macroxiphus" kingdom="Animalia" order="Orthoptera" pageId="6" pageNumber="123" phylum="Arthropoda" rank="subSpecies" species="sumatranus" subSpecies="sumatranus">
<emphasis id="E1E7EAE5FFA85D4F4C4BF98A2822F99A" italics="true" pageId="6" pageNumber="123">Macroxiphus sumatranus sumatranus</emphasis>
</taxonomicName>
(recorded from Maninjau from West Sumatra), whereas that of 
<taxonomicName id="14934D74FFA85D4F4C30F9A62CA4F99A" authorityName="Helfert &amp; Sanger" authorityYear="1995" box="[1029,1436,1578,1604]" class="Insecta" family="Tettigoniidae" genus="Macroxiphus" kingdom="Animalia" order="Orthoptera" pageId="6" pageNumber="123" phylum="Arthropoda" rank="subSpecies" species="sumatranus" subSpecies="siamensis">
<emphasis id="E1E7EAE5FFA85D4F4C30F9A62CA4F99A" box="[1029,1436,1578,1604]" italics="true" pageId="6" pageNumber="123">Macroxiphus sumatranus siamensis</emphasis>
</taxonomicName>
(recorded from Ulu Gombak in Selangor and 
<collectingRegion id="1157F815FFA85D4F4AA3F9C22A21F9B1" box="[662,793,1614,1640]" country="Thailand" name="Surat Thani" pageId="6" pageNumber="123">Surat Thani</collectingRegion>
in 
<collectingCountry id="AB847667FFA85D4F4B09F9C22A99F9B1" box="[828,929,1614,1640]" name="Thailand" pageId="6" pageNumber="123">Thailand</collectingCountry>
) typically consists of four syllables.
</paragraph>
